  "details": {
    "note": "brief 072-F (Vela's design, briefs/072/texture/design.md): the kit detail pairs a colour surface's `detail` names. Colourless (albedo x2 about 128 and a tangent normal), laid in URP Lit's own detail slots with _DETAIL_MULX2 on box-projected UVs in metres, so the colour stays the surface's. tile = metres per repeat, bump = _DetailNormalMapScale [S]. glass, water and crossing take none (transparent glazing, the Water shader, the signal-adjacent crossing).",
    "limestone": { "albedo": "surface_limestone_detail_v1", "normal": "surface_limestone_detail_v1_normal", "tile": 2.0, "bump": 0.3 },
    "enamel": { "albedo": "surface_enamel_detail_v1", "normal": "surface_enamel_detail_v1_normal", "tile": 1.0, "bump": 0.25 },
